Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Image Pull Errors

Problem: Pods stuck in ImagePullBackOff state
Solution: Ensure the Docker image is loaded into the kind cluster using kind load docker-image
Issue 2: Template Rendering Errors

Problem: Helm template syntax errors
Solution: Use helm template command to debug template rendering and check YAML indentation
Issue 3: Service Not Accessible

Problem: Cannot access the service externally
Solution: For kind clusters, use NodePort services or port-forwarding for testing
Issue 4: Resource Limits

Problem: Pods being killed due to resource constraints
Solution: Adjust resource limits in values files based on your system capabilities
